# Narrowly scoped: preserved benchmark evidence must stay byte-exact on every
# platform. Without this, core.autocrlf normalises the CRLF line endings these
# files were written with and every recorded SHA-256 stops matching.
#
# `binary` is `-text -diff -merge`: it pins the bytes AND stops Git from treating
# the preserved CR line endings as trailing whitespace, which would make
# `git diff --check` fail on every line of frozen evidence. These files are never
# edited, so losing textual diffs on them costs nothing.
#
# This deliberately does NOT change the project's text rules for any other path.
artifacts/benchmark_v6/** binary
